The legal texts are the Constitution of the Russian Federation, as published by the Official Internet Portal
of Legal Information (pravo.gov.ru), system "Законодательство России" (actual.pravo.gov.ru), retrieved 29 October 2026.

Official texts of laws are not protected by copyright in Russia: Civil Code of the Russian Federation,
art. 1259(6) ("Не являются объектами авторских прав ... официальные документы государственных органов ...,
в том числе законы, другие нормативные акты, судебные решения ...") - official documents, including laws and other
normative acts, are not objects of copyright.

Changes made by Lexifina: each edition was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per line;
the portal's amendment notes were left out of the text; one missing full stop in article 55(1) of the portal's
editions of 1996 to 2019 was restored from the original and current text; and the editions were arranged as git
commits credited to the decrees and laws that made each change. The wording of the law was not otherwise changed.
The portal does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools)
are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
